Z||000015||Standard||01-15-2000||05:06 AM||||So you're that WebElectric guy!  I found a link to your site from somewhere (can't remember where) and was really impressed with it.  Really liked that big brake article.  You do good work!  Welcome to the forum!||||reg||14
Z||000016||lawrence||01-15-2000||09:11 AM||||Monkeyman,<P>My medication is a light golden color and comes in a green bottle.<P>Standard,<P>Thanks for the nice comments.  I started that mag almost two years ago and I love doing it.  However, sometimes it takes a lot of time and effort to get it out on time.  For the next issue, I'm working on a new dome light extender that will dim the lights as it turns off.  I have the circuit designed and breadboarded, but I don't know when I'll have time to install it in a vehicle to check it out.  One thing I've found over the years is that if it works on the bench, so what.  You need to put it in the field, especially when you are talking about circuits for cars.<P>Have fun,<P>-L||||reg||1
Z||000017||Phil||01-15-2000||05:28 PM||||My Plymouth Laser has that delay dome light and it sure is a nice feature. You can shut the door and still have time to find the keyhole before it gets dark. Before anyone says anything YES it works better at night ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Monkeyman||01-15-2000||06:54 PM||||My wifes '98 Cav has the dome light thing.  It's one of the few things I really like about her car.  ||||reg||1
